in{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrices $P$ and $Q$ are not elementary matrices because they can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\n- The matrix $S$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =S\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $S$ is an elementary matrix." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130772/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130772"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-42751/selection/afe4b97c823938f24ee0f462e6dae1ce1a6e74074abfb6f3f9af3b253499f0cc" :answer/id #uuid "42f6c261-4717-5cae-a78c-325aed2aa77c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42751/selection/de626a209cc5a46a5d421556cdfa477e78a24e22bc848d759ca1def3272edc4d" :answer/id #uuid "1bb79d30-f760-5444-ad9f-91e29a499a03" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$Q$ and $E$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42751/selection/bc3f7329f2aae1f9796f8a47cb28b4414aa963daad38c56d171d11cbcbe5af2d" :answer/id #uuid "9a0564f8-c169-5ed9-a7ed-388dfe1ae943" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$W$ and $E$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42751/selection/7dac0ad80ece25ffc25e933add4a53b1577f76de4cc80d106d927934a5c71ea3" :answer/id #uuid "47994b21-