wer-fields ["q-130778/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130778"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130774/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "a3b5f78f-1e63-5800-ae3e-5d8f9a18d9bc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130774/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "8968f30f-7a08-5194-b917-09339fb2dc5a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130774/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "b0d8bddf-f629-504e-aa49-6e2b13c5c5f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130774/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "3dc2ff11-20a9-50aa-bf2b-98fa5d5b517f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130774/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "14c2de26-a3a9-5bf4-b032-07d4f0db7642" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130774/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ddb4f9c-b793-51c0-9fde-49a175491b33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-130774/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-130774/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-130774/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" "q-130774/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-130774/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-130774/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-130774" :question/id #uuid "17df8f70-560c-50cc-995c-b38203b5ea8b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130774" :question/problem "Which of the following are elementary matrices?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An elementary matrix is a matrix obtained from the identity matrix by applying exactly one elementary row operation. \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our matrices.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is an elementary matrix because it can be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}↔{R}_{2},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not an elementary matrix because it can't be obtained from ${I}_{2}$ by applying only one elementary row operation.\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are elementary matrices." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130774/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "853a04b2-591a-51c2-b80f-73f559355d9f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130774"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73646/selection/116ba511f78f3ed888236c80aa0db20008860383f2b4